0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>June to August</strong><span class="t">47% of the income</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Oceanfront condos for sale, Myrtle Beach</strong><span class="t">95% marked nightly</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>Myrtle Beach neighborhoods</strong><span class="t">Mostly lease only</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated June 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Run it yourself, and a two-bedroom Airbnb leaves you more than a lease once guests book it about 82 nights a year. Most city neighborhoods allow only a lease.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An Airbnb, if you run it yourself and guests book it a third of the nights in the year. The owner of a Myrtle Beach two-bedroom then keeps about $8,000 a year more than with a lease. Many listings book fewer nights, and the owner of the middle two-bedroom listing keeps about $3,000 less than with a lease.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Of 422 condos for sale in oceanfront buildings inside Myrtle Beach city limits, listing agents marked 402 as allowing nightly stays. Most city neighborhoods allow only stays of 90 days or more.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Send us one address. We run it both ways before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us run both numbers</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#which-earns-more" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which earns more</a></li><li><a href="#is-it-allowed" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Is it allowed</a></li><li><a href="#break-even" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Nights to break even</a></li><li><a href="#month-by-month" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Month by month</a></li><li><a href="#pros-and-cons" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Pros and cons</a></li><li><a href="#what-we-do" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What we do</a></li><li><a href="#airbnb-vs-long-term-rental-questions" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Airbnb vs long-term rental questions</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="which-earns-more"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Which earns more">Which earns more in Myrtle Beach, an Airbnb or a long-term rental?</h2><style>
